00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:27,000
Does it make a difference if you were taking it for diabetes versus just for weight loss

295
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,080
in terms of what happens when you stop?

296
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:32,279
Yes, there are some differences in the primary concerns.

297
00:12:32,279 --> 00:12:36,840
For someone with type 2 diabetes, the biggest immediate issue when stopping is losing that

298
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:38,360
blood sugar control.

299
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:40,759
Their A1C will likely go up.

300
00:12:40,759 --> 00:12:42,960
Does managing blood sugar is so critical?

301
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:46,279
These patients might be more likely to restart the therapy or switch to another diabetes

302
00:12:46,279 --> 00:12:47,960
medication fairly quickly.

303
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:52,120
For people using it purely for weight loss who usually have normal blood sugar to begin

304
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:57,120
with, the main consequence of stopping is that significant weight regain.

305
00:12:57,120 --> 00:13:00,759
And losing those improvements in blood pressure, lipids, and so on.

306
00:13:00,759 --> 00:13:05,259
Discontinuation rates tend to be higher in this group, often because of cost or maybe side

307
00:13:05,259 --> 00:13:09,399
effects becoming too bothersome without the added driver of diabetes control.

308
00:13:10,399 --> 00:13:13,759
That paints a much clearer picture of the long-term reality.

